      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not support the claim that the serotonin reuptake transporter is a “serotonin-related protein” nor that it is “used here as a marker” for serotonin-producing nerve cells; it only states that Cre recombinase was “driven by the 5-HT-specific serotonin reuptake transporter (SERT) promoter.”",
        "The packet supports that the SERT promoter was used to selectively target 5-HT neurons (via Cre recombinase), but the definition’s first sentence adds additional, unsupported characterization (marker role and protein description)."
